- An image which is published is *sealed*: it is compact, it carries its value hash and its
- digests, and it is never changed. The program which owns a document keeps a working copy of
- it, which it changes where it lies. A file is opened for that with `Read & Write`, which
- holds an exclusive lock on it, and the block's reader then changes records as well as reading
- them:
+ Una imagen que se publica está *sellada*: es compacta, lleva su hash de valor y sus resúmenes,
+ y nunca se modifica. El programa que es dueño de un documento guarda una copia de trabajo de
+ él, que modifica allí donde está. Para ello, un fichero se abre con `Read & Write`, que
+ mantiene sobre él un bloqueo exclusivo, y el lector del bloque entonces modifica registros
+ además de leerlos:

